ion: Caroline passed adoption agency interviews last Friday, viewing adoption as a way to build her family, give back, and show love and acceptance.\n  - people: Caroline applied to adoption agencies, attended an adoption advice group, and went hiking, later apologizing to some people she had an issue with. She previously considered counseling and mental health jobs.\n  - Mel: Melanie (Mel) congratulated Caroline on passing adoption agency interviews. She supports Caroline's goal of building a family through adoption to help needy kids.\n  - adoption advice/assistance group: Caroline attended an adoption advice/assistance group this week to get help for her decision to apply to adoption agencies to become a mom.\n  - adoption process: Caroline mentioned an adoption process and Melanie expressed support and asked about what Caroline is excited for regarding it.\n  - Melanie: Melanie congratulated Caroline on passing adoption agency interviews, viewing adoption as a loving way to build a family for needy kids, and encouraged Caroline to be herself.\n  - adoption agency interviews: Caroline passed the adoption agency interviews last Friday and is excited about this step towards having a family.\n  - understanding and acceptance: Caroline aims to spread understanding and acceptance by building a family through adoption, following successful agency interviews last Friday.\n  - adoption journey: Caroline passed adoption agency interviews last Friday, a major step toward her goal of building a family and giving a home to needy kids.\n  - support: Caroline values support from friends and family, and now aims to give back by offering comfort and help to others, similar to her past gratifying experience volunteering at an LGBTQ+ youth center.\n  - inclusivity and support: Melanie expressed appreciation for the inclusivity and support mentioned by Caroline and inquired about Caroline's excitement regarding the adoption process.\n  - support groups: Caroline was inspired by cou